add('1779-Q03','sourceSupport','The sole cited page labels the torso device Intel RealSense D435i for nonverbal interaction, but does not explicitly identify its RGB/depth channels or downstream inference boundary. Add page1782 for the RGB/depth hardware annotation and page1781 or1784 for camera versus DeepFace responsibilities, keeping the original annotated-device reference.')
add('1784-Q03','distractors','Replace the seven-output-classes therefore seven-image-input-channels alternative with a credible same-domain input-representation misconception. The RGB-D therefore four classifier channels alternative is useful; the unrelated output-count inference is conspicuous filler. Preserve the key that the exact downstream tensor is not established by the diagram.')
add('1785-Q05','distractors','Both wrong alternatives deny feature extraction altogether: terminal argmax supposedly replaces the convolution hierarchy, or deeper layers can only retain raw pixels. Use plausible contrasting learned-feature hierarchies, receptive-field/composition assumptions or localization-versus-classification stages instead of two extreme negations of the definition.')
add('1786-Q02','distractors','Both wrong alternatives posit unspecified per-crop retraining or weight updates, with little distinct reasoning between them. Keep one meaningful inference-versus-training confusion and replace the other with a plausible frozen-model feature/output interpretation. Do not imply a change of internal state can never occur in software; the question is about the stated learned-parameter inference stage.')
add('1789-Q04','distractors','The two distractors restate essentially the same claim that event types have no meaning. Replace one or the whole recall item with a bounded stateful event trace in which speech-start, old-response audio and playback queue transitions must be distinguished. Explicitly supply any policy or API-event behavior not printed by the course; this can address L56-G01.')
add('1794-Q01','distractors','Use comparable complete paths through the actual lower-row nodes. The current wrong paths invent a human-output-to-camera loop or skip directly from emotion to speaker rather than competing interpretations of the lower-row arrow order. Preserve the correct right-to-left source reading; do not turn the functional speech/language boxes into a mandatory internal API model cascade.')
add('1798-Q03','explanation','The first working step lists ages0.25,0.50,0.10s without labels, whereas current option order o1/o2/o3 has ages0.50,0.10,0.25s. Bind each calculation to its option or observation rather than leaving a stale permutation. The key and each option rationale are correct.')
add('1798-Q05','duplication','This repeats the exact local-perception/cloud-dialogue distinction already tested by P1782-Q02; changing the wording to an outage does not add a decision rule or new dependency. Replace it with an integrated resource/fallback decision, for example L56-G02, while retaining the earlier architectural split question.')
